ocess. ',70,'MEDIUM','2026-01-11 19:47:48.720591',32,30,13,10,'NEUTRAL'),(71,90,'The main difference is thread safety: HashMap is not thread-safe (faster, single-threaded use), while ConcurrentHashMap is thread-safe (slower, multi-threaded use) but handles concurrent modifications gracefully without ConcurrentModificationException, using fine-grained locking (segmentation/striping) instead of locking the whole map, allowing better concurrency than older synchronized maps. HashMap allows one null key/values, but ConcurrentHashMap does not allow any null keys or values. ',85,'HIGH','2026-01-11 19:47:54.548328',32,90,3,95,'POSITIVE'),(72,85,'\nObject-Oriented Programming (OOP) in Java is a programming paradigm that organizes code around objects rather than functions. It is built upon the core concepts of Encapsulation, Inheritance, Polymorphism, and Abstraction, along with the fundamental ideas of classes and objects. ',80,'MEDIUM','2026-01-11 19:47:59.078499',32,85,2,90,'POSITIVE'),(73,80,'Spring Boot is an open-source framework built on top of the existing Spring framework that simplifies the creation of standalone, production-grade applications with minimal configuration. It helps developers build Java-based applications, such as microservices and web apps, faster and more efficiently by reducing boilerplate code and configuration complexity. ',75,'MEDIUM','2026-01-11 19:48:03.736508',32,80,6,85,'POSITIVE'),(74,20,'\"Collections in Java\" refers to the Java Collections Framework, a unified architecture within the java.util package that provides interfaces, implementations (classes), and algorithms for storing and manipulating groups of objects. ',70,'MEDIUM','2026-01-11 19:48:08.582478',32,33.33,11,10,'NEUTRAL'),(75,0,'aa',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:03:38.874078',33,0,5,0,'NEGATIVE'),(76,0,'dd',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:03:43.629227',33,0,3,0,'NEGATIVE'),(77,0,'fh',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:03:46.351126',33,0,12,0,'NEGATIVE'),(78,0,'fg',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:03:49.970849',33