es code around objects rather than functions. It is built upon the core concepts of Encapsulation, Inheritance, Polymorphism, and Abstraction, along with the fundamental ideas of classes and objects. ',80,'MEDIUM','2026-01-11 20:33:17.000700',36,85,2,90,'POSITIVE'),(94,20,'Multithreading in Java is a feature that allows multiple threads of execution to run concurrently within a single program, maximizing CPU utilization and improving application responsiveness. Each thread is a lightweight, independent sub-process that shares the same memory space as the parent process. ',70,'MEDIUM','2026-01-11 20:33:21.474064',36,33.33,13,10,'NEUTRAL'),(95,0,'aa',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:36:42.165361',37,0,3,0,'NEGATIVE'),(96,0,'fg',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:36:45.786540',37,2,6,0,'NEGATIVE'),(97,0,'dg',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:36:49.738012',37,0,13,0,'NEGATIVE'),(98,0,'dg',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:36:52.801111',37,2,11,0,'NEGATIVE'),(99,0,'g',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:36:57.859571',37,0,5,0,'NEGATIVE'),(100,0,'aa',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:44:45.167688',38,2,12,0,'NEGATIVE'),(101,0,'gg',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:44:48.384782',38,2.5,13,0,'NEGATIVE'),(102,0,'dg',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:44:51.315722',38,0,5,0,'NEGATIVE'),(103,0,'ga',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:44:54.951384',38,0,11,0,'NEGATIVE'),(104,0,'dg',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:44:59.718547',38,2,2,0,'NEGATIVE'),(105,0,'ss',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:52:45.610441',39,0,11,0,'NEGATIVE'),(106,0,'df',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:52:49.974999',39,0,5,0,'NEGATIVE'),(107,0,'df',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:52:53.684838',39,2,13,0,'NEGATIVE'),(108,0,'dgd',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:52:57.407043',39,2,2,0,'NEGATIVE'),(109,0,'dgadd',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:53:01.030094',39,2,12,0,'NEGATIVE'),(110,0,'ss',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:56:48.153005',40,0,13,0,'NEGATIVE'),(111,0,'dg',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:56:51.680847',40,0,6,0,'NEGATIVE'),(112,0,'dg',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:56:56.556234',40,2,12,0,'NEGATIVE'),(113,0,'d',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:56:59.425094',40,0,5,0,'NEGATIVE'),(114,0,'d',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 20:57:04.641385',40,2,2,0,'NEGATIVE'),(115,0,'aa',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:03:23.890679',41,2,13,0,'NEGATIVE'),(116,0,'fg',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:03:27.540760',41,2,2,0,'NEGATIVE'),(117,0,'df',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:03:31.416858',41,0,3,0,'NEGATIVE'),(118,0,'df',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:03:35.750052',41,2,5,0,'NEGATIVE'),(119,0,'df',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:03:39.008586',41,2,12,0,'NEGATIVE'),(120,0,'dd',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:11:15.565882',42,0,3,0,'NEGATIVE'),(121,0,'dag',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:11:20.173183',42,2,13,0,'NEGATIVE'),(122,0,'gaaaa',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:11:25.094731',42,2,2,0,'NEGATIVE'),(123,0,'daf',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:11:29.211892',42,2,12,0,'NEGATIVE'),(124,0,'daf',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:11:43.337686',42,2,6,0,'NEGATIVE'),(125,85,'\nObject-Oriented Programming (OOP) is a programming paradigm that organizes code around objects, which are instances of classes that combine both data (attributes) and behavior (methods) into a single unit. The core principles of OOP in Java are Abstraction, Encapsulation, Inheritance, and Polymorphism, often referred to as the \"Four Pillars\". ',80,'HIGH','2026-01-11 21:26:09.361187',43,85,2,90,'POSITIVE'),(126,80,'Spring Boot is an extension of the Spring framework that streamlines and speeds up the development of standalone, production-grade Java applications with minimal configuration. It significantly reduces the boilerplate code and manual setup traditionally required for Spring projects, allowing developers to focus on business logic. ',90,'HIGH','2026-01-11 21:26:13.343171',43,85,6,85,'POSITIVE'),(127,20,'The term \"collections\" in Java primarily refers to the Java Collections Framework (JCF), a unified architecture for representing and manipulating groups of objects. It includes a set of interfaces, implementations (classes), and algorithms in the java.util package. ',70,'MEDIUM','2026-01-11 21:26:17.422468',43,35,11,15,'NEUTRAL'),(128,90,'The main difference is thread safety: HashMap is not thread-safe (faster, single-threaded use), while ConcurrentHashMap is thread-safe (slower, multi-threaded use) but handles concurrent modifications gracefully without ConcurrentModificationException, using fine-grained locking (segmentation/striping) instead of locking the whole map, allowing better concurrency than older synchronized maps. HashMap allows one null key/values, but ConcurrentHashMap does not allow any null keys or values.',85,'HIGH','2026-01-11 21:26:21.584769',43,90,3,95,'POSITIVE'),(129,90,'The main difference is thread safety: HashMap is not thread-safe (faster, single-threaded use), while ConcurrentHashMap is thread-safe (slower, multi-threaded use) but handles concurrent modifications gracefully without ConcurrentModificationException, using fine-grained locking (segmentation/striping) instead of locking the whole map, allowing better concurrency than older synchronized maps. HashMap allows one null key/values, but ConcurrentHashMap does not allow any null keys or values.',85,'HIGH','2026-01-11 21:26:24.360920',43,90,3,95,'POSITIVE'),(130,50,'Exception handling is a programming technique to manage runtime errors (exceptions) that disrupt a program\'s normal flow, preventing crashes by using try, catch, and finally blocks to detect, handle, or clean up after unexpected events like division by zero or file errors, ensuring code robustness and graceful exits. It allows developers to isolate potentially problematic code, \"catch\" specific errors, execute alternative logic, and release resources, keeping the application stable. ',70,'MEDIUM','2026-01-11 21:26:25.657968',43,53.33,12,40,'NEUTRAL'),(131,60,'Exception handling is a programming technique to manage runtime errors (exceptions) that disrupt a program\'s normal flow, preventing crashes by using try, catch, and finally blocks to detect, handle, or clean up after unexpected events like division by zero or file errors, ensuring code robustness and graceful exits. It allows developers to isolate potentially problematic code, \"catch\" specific errors, execute alternative logic, and release resources, keeping the application stable. ',70,'MEDIUM','2026-01-11 21:26:27.845504',43,60,12,50,'NEUTRAL'),(132,0,'aa',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:33:51.684715',44,0,13,0,'NEGATIVE'),(133,0,'dv',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:33:56.343612',44,2,12,0,'NEGATIVE'),(134,0,'sd',0,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:34:00.003166',44,0,3,0,'NEGATIVE'),(135,0,'sd',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:34:03.674969',44,2,2,0,'NEGATIVE'),(136,0,'sd',10,'LOW','2026-01-11 21:34:08.968033',44,2,11,0,'NEGATIVE'),(137,90,'The main difference is thread safety: HashMap is not thread-safe (faster, single-threaded use), while ConcurrentHashMap is thread-safe (slower, multi-threaded use) but handles concurrent modifications gracefully without ConcurrentModificationException, using fine-grained locking (segmentation/striping) instead of locking the whole map, allowing better concurrency than older synchronized maps. HashMap allows one null key/values, but ConcurrentHashMap does not allow any null keys or values. ',85,'HIGH','2026-01-11 21:39:41.798202',45,90,3,95,'POSITIVE'),(138,40,'The term \"collections\" in Java primarily refers to the Java Collections Framework (JCF), a unified architecture for representing and manipulating groups of objects. It includes a set of interfaces, implementations (classes), and algorithms in the java.util package. \nThe framework provides reusable data structures like dynamic arrays, linked lists, hash tables, and trees, which are more flexible than traditional arrays. ',70,'MEDIUM','2026-01-11 21:39:45.748894',45,46,11,30,'NEUTRAL'),(139,85,'Spring Boot is an extension of the Spring framework that streamlines and speeds up the development of standalone, production-grade Java applications with minimal configuration. It significantly reduces the boilerplate code and manual setup traditionally required for Spring projects, allowing developers to focus on business logic. ',90,'HIGH','202